        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12444267/comment/12795340",
          "id": "12795340",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "The justification for using @Deprecated, AFAICT, is that conforming compilers are required to issue warnings for each so-annotated class/method, where compilers are *not* required to issue warnings for javadoc @deprecated tags, and although Sun compilers do this, other vendors' compilers might not.\n\nAnother (similarly theoretical) argument in favor of using @Deprecated annotations is that, unlike @deprecated javadoc tags, this annotation is available via runtime reflection.\n\nA random information point: MYFACES-2135 removed all @Deprecated annotations from MyFaces code because an apparent bug in the Sun TCK flags methods bearing this annotation as changing method signatures.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-12-30T16:17:17.340+0000",
          "updated": "2009-12-30T16:17:17.340+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12444267/comment/12795342",
          "id": "12795342",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Steven, yeah i know theoretically why this is here, but it is completely stupid.\n\n@Deprecated is a gigantic mistake, requiring me to write it twice, once lowercase in the javadocs, once uppercase as an annotation. This is the only way to properly deprecate something with a message as to why.\n\nand so this additional work buys me nothing, except some theoretical workaround to sun's piss-poor broken language design.\n\nthis being said, i still think we should be consistent: either remove all these annotations or add them all, and not just use them 'sometime'.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-12-30T16:23:58.305+0000",
          "updated": "2009-12-30T16:23:58.305+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12444267/comment/12795962",
          "id": "12795962",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
